[{:db/id -1, :doc/id "doc-ayatori-bench-coscientist-iteration-23", :doc/title "ayatori Co-Scientist Iteration 23 — the named reference over every parameter: eight served reads, zero disagreements with Neo4j", :doc/path "bench/coscientist-iteration-23.edn", :doc/body "# Co-Scientist iteration 23 - the named reference over every parameter: eight served reads, zero disagreements with Neo4j\n\n> Seed: iteration 22's S12 - the four short reads were gated by two\n> independent implementations agreeing, not by the Neo4j pairing the\n> benchmark names. Judge: bench/benchmark.edn v2, gate :answers-agree-\n> with-reference.\n\n## Generate\n\n  ldbc-snb-bench gains Cypher IS2/IS4/IS5/IS7 (the root post via\n  `[:REPLY_OF*0..]` to a message with no REPLY_OF; the IS7 knows flag as\n  `EXISTS { (a)-[:KNOWS]-(ma) }`) and `reference-agreement`: with a\n  params dir, every served read is compared with Neo4j over every\n  official parameter and the subset's short-read messages -- not only\n  the first start person, which is all the harness had checked before.\n  Ordered rows for IC02/IC08/IS2/IS4/IS5/IS7; IC07 liker sets and IC09\n  message sets (creationDate ties at the limit boundary), as before.\n\n  Prediction: zero disagreements on every op (the index twins had\n  already agreed on 787 parameters, and the Datalog side is what the\n  Neo4j gate compares).\n\n## Rank (simeon, one JVM with both engines, -Xmx12g, SUT stopped)\n\n    op    checked  disagreements\n    ic02     98        0           is2   98   0\n    ic07     98        0           is4   99   0\n    ic08     98        0           is5   99   0\n    ic09     98        0           is7   99   0\n\n  Paired p50 ratio kotobase / Neo4j on the 15 highest-degree persons:\n    ic02 0.28   ic07 1.31   ic08 2.32   ic09 0.85\n  (2026-08-14 receipt: 3.07 / 0.84 / 1.96 / 7.38)\n  Absolute p50: ic09 kotobase 50.5 ms, Neo4j 59.2.\n\n## Reflect\n\n  - Held. The iteration 22 rows now carry the reference the benchmark\n    names; the gap they stated is closed by a row, not by editing them.\n  - Not sought, but measured: the ordered drive (19) and the planner\n    cache (20) turned the in-process comparison over. IC02 is 3.6x\n    faster than embedded Neo4j and IC09 1.2x; IC07/IC08 are sub-\n    millisecond on both sides. That is the same paired harness, same\n    machine class, same data rule as the August receipts.\n  - The harness compared the first start person for three months; the\n    all-parameter check took an afternoon. A gate that runs on one\n    input is a gate that has been shown to pass once.\n\n## Meta\n\nVerdict under bench/benchmark.edn v2: REFERENCE-ESTABLISHED (no\nthroughput row; the gate for 8 of 29 operations holds on every\nparameter). M1 stands at 8/29 served with reference, 0 with updates.\n\nSeeds for iteration 24, in order:\n\n  - S13 (subset attributes): load person profile fields, friendship\n    creationDate and forums so IS1/IS3/IS6 and the IC reads that need\n    them have data; each addition is quads, and the per-quad footprint\n    is the M3 number.\n  - S11 (per-op cost): server threads 10 vs 8, EDN printing, the\n    drive's independent half as sets (IC09 at 50 ms dense).\n  - M2 (updates): the eight inserts on a transacting SUT -- the design\n    step.\n"}]
